ntent="#203f39"><link rel="icon" href="/assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="th" href="https://takuapa101.com/routes/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/routes/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://takuapa101.com/routes/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="Takua Pa 101 Home"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="เมนูหลัก"><a href="/en/places/">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/">Stories</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" aria-current="page" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">Leaflet</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/routes/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><a class="lang-switch" href="/en/routes/" hreflang="en" lang="en">EN</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="สลับเป็นโหมดกลางคืน"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="Open menu"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="Search website (Press Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="Your trip"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="intro"><a class="eyebrow" href="/en/">Takua Pa 101 / Old Town Guide</a><h1>Choose your walking pace</h1><p class="lead">Three sets of destinations that invite you to see Takua Pa through different stories</p></div><p class="route-notice">Grouped by interest, no distance or walking time set. Check visiting info and use the map before traveling</p><div class="route-jumps"><a href="#route-1">01 / Temples and chedis route</a><a href="#route-2">02 / Shrines and vegetarian halls route</a><a href="#route-3">03 / Old buildings and riverside market route</a><a href="#route-4">04 / Short walk from the wooden house</a></div><section class="route-chapter" id="route-1"><div class="route-chapter-visual"><span class="giant-number">01</span><img src="/assets/wat-boromthat.webp" alt="Wat Boromthat Khiri Khet (the town&#x27;s relic temple)" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="chapter">TAKUA PA / WALK & READ</span></div><div class="route-chapter-copy"><h2>Temples and Pagodas Route</h2><ol class="stops"><li><span>01</span><div><h3><a href="/en/places/wat-boromthat/">Wat Boromthat Khiri Khet (the town's relic temple)</a></h3><p>White pagoda and the town's faith</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><h3><a href="/en/places/wat-khuha/">Wat Khuha Phimuk (the cave hill temple)</a></h3><p>Small details that invite you to pause and look.</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><h3><a href="/en/places/wat-pathum/">Wat Pathum Thara (the front town temple)</a></h3><p>Old ordination hall and waterway stories</p></div></li><li><span>04</span><div><h3><a href="/en/places/wat-kongkha/">Wat Kongkha Phimuk (the riverside temple)</a></h3><p>Southern Thai style ordination hall details</p></div></li><li><span>05</span><div><h3><a href="/en/places/wat-nikorn/">Wat Nikornwararam</a></h3><p>The temple and community memories</p></div></li><li><span>06</span><div><h3><a href="/en/places/wat-sena/">Wat Sena Nuch Rangsan</a></h3><p>Thai and Chinese traces in the same building</p></div></li></ol><a class="text-link" href="/en/map/">Open reference map ↗</a></div></section><section class="route-chapter" id="route-2"><div class="route-chapter-visual"><span class="giant-number">02</span><img src="/assets/guan-yu.webp" alt="Guan Yu / Sin Chai Tung Shrine" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="chapter">TAKUA PA / WALK & READ</span></div><div class="route-chapter-copy"><h2>Shrines and Vegetarian Halls Route</h2><ol class="stops"><li><span>01</span><div><h3><a href="/en/places/guan-yu/">Guan Yu / Sin Chai Tung Shrine</a></h3><p>Red door and the community's faith</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><h3><a href="/en/places/pun-thao/">Pun Thao Kong A Shrine</a></h3><p>Faith in the old port area</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><h3><a href="/en/places/kue-chai/">Kue Chai Tung Shrine</a></h3><p>A space for people's hopes</p></div></li><li><span>04</span><div><h3><a href="/en/places/rong-jae/">The Shrine in the Garden</a></h3><p>Traditions passed down through places</p></div></li></ol><a class="text-link" href="/en/map/">Open reference map ↗</a></div></section><section class="route-chapter" id="route-3"><div class="route-chapter-visual"><span class="giant-number">03</span><img src="/assets/tao-ming.webp" alt="Tao Ming School" width="1000" height="667" loading="lazy"><span class="chapter">TAKUA PA / WALK & READ</span></div><div class="route-chapter-copy"><h2>Old Buildings and Riverside Market Route</h2><ol class="stops"><li><span>01</span><div><h3><a href="/en/places/tao-ming/">Tao Ming School</a></h3><p>A building that passes on language and culture</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><h3><a href="/en/places/khun-in/">Khun In House</a></h3><p>Windows and balconies inviting a look into the past</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><h3><a href="/en/places/governor-wall/">Governor’s Residence Wall</a></h3><p>A trace on the wall that tells the town's story</p></div></li><li><span>04</span><div><h3><a href="/en/places/culture-street/">Takua Pa Old Town Cultural Street</a></h3><p>Walking and reading the city through buildings and people</p></div></li><li><span>05</span><div><h3><a href="/en/places/riverwalk/">Takuapa Riverwalk</a></h3><p>Food and life by the river</p></div></li><li><span>06</span><div><h3><a href="/en/places/food-center/">Takua Pa Open-Air Food Center</a></h3><p>Many flavors in one destination</p></div></li></ol><a class="text-link" href="/en/map/">Open reference map ↗</a></div></section><section class="route-chapter" id="route-4"><div class="route-chapter-visual"><span class="giant-number">04</span><img src="/assets/khun-in.webp" alt="Khun In House" width="1000" height="1000" loading="lazy"><span class="chapter">TAKUA PA / WALK & READ</span></div><div class="route-chapter-copy"><h2>Short walk from wooden house</h2><ol class="stops"><li><span>01</span><div><h3><a href="/en/places/khun-in/">Khun In House</a></h3><p>Windows and balconies inviting a look into the past</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><h3><a href="/en/places/tao-ming/">Tao Ming School</a></h3><p>A building that passes on language and culture</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><h3><a href="/en/places/guan-yu/">Guan Yu / Sin Chai Tung Shrine</a></h3><p>Red door and the community's faith</p></div></li><li><span>04</span><div><h3><a href="/en/places/iron-bridge/">Boon Soong Iron Bridge</a></h3><p>Iron structure connecting mining stories</p></div></li></ol><a class="text-link" href="/en/map/">Open reference map ↗</a></div></section><aside class="source"><h2>Data Sources</h2><p>Compiled from<a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Takua Pa Town Municipality brochure</a> · Data extracted September 6, 2026 (2569 BE). The document does not specify a publication date. Opening hours, shop status, and current schedules are not verified. Please check with the venue before traveling.</p></aside></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="Back to top">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="Quick menu"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
.\audit\jobs\en-attrs.log:884:D:\Siwaracafeweb\output\web\takuapa101-v1\site\en\stories\index.html:1:<!doctype html><html lang="en" data-base="" data-news-api=""><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>Stories of Takua Pa: History, Tin and the River · Takua Pa 101</title><meta name="description" content="Long reads on how Takua Pa grew: the river that moved the town, buildings paid for with tin money, Peranakan food, and the old town waking up again."><meta name="robots" content="index,follow,max-image-preview:large"><meta property="og:title" content="Stories of Takua Pa: History, Tin and the River"><meta property="og:description" content="Long reads on how Takua Pa grew: the river that moved the town, buildings paid for with tin money, Peranakan food, and the old town waking up again."><meta property="og:url" content="https://takuapa101.com/stories/"><meta property="og:type" content="website"><meta property="og:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/default.png"><meta property="og:locale" content="en_US"><meta property="og:site_name" content="Takua Pa 101"><meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"><meta name="twitter:image" content="https://takuapa101.com/assets/og/default.png"><meta name="generator" content="Takua Pa 101"><link rel="canonical" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/stories/"><link rel="preload" href="/assets/NotoSerifThai.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="preload" href="/assets/IBMPlexSansThaiLooped-Regular.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/design.css"><script type="application/ld+json">[{"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Takua Pa Stories", "item": "https://takuapa101.com/stories/"}]}, {"@context": "https://schema.org", "inLanguage": "en", "@type": "ItemList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "url": "https://takuapa101.com/stories/city/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "url": "https://takuapa101.com/stories/architecture/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "url": "https://takuapa101.com/stories/water-trade/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 4, "url": "https://takuapa101.com/stories/food-people/"}, {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 5, "url": "https://takuapa101.com/stories/kuapapoh/"}]}]</script><script src="/assets/design.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/trip.js" defer></script><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/ui.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/theme.css"><script src="/assets/theme.js"></script><script src="/assets/search.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/live-news.js" defer></script><meta name="theme-color" content="#203f39"><link rel="icon" href="/assets/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="th" href="https://takuapa101.com/stories/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="en" href="https://takuapa101.com/en/stories/"><link rel="alternate" hreflang="x-default" href="https://takuapa101.com/stories/"></head><body class="inner-page"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header"><a class="brand" href="/en/" aria-label="Takua Pa 101 Home"><span class="brand-mark">101</span><span>Takua Pa<small>TAKUA PA FIELD NOTES</small></span></a><nav id="main-nav" aria-label="เมนูหลัก"><a href="/en/places/">Places</a><a href="/en/stories/" aria-current="page">Stories</a><a href="/en/map/">Map</a><a href="/en/rest/">Eat and explore</a><a href="/en/news/">Updates</a><a href="/en/trip/">Your trip</a><a href="/en/traditions/" class="nav-more">Traditions</a><a href="/en/eat/" class="nav-more">Eat & Souvenirs</a><a href="/en/routes/" class="nav-more">Walking Routes</a><a href="/en/leaflet/" class="nav-more">Leaflet</a><a href="/en/about/" class="nav-more">About</a></nav><div class="header-tools"><a class="lang-switch" href="/stories/" hreflang="th" lang="th">ไทย</a><a class="lang-switch" href="/en/stories/" hreflang="en" lang="en">EN</a><button class="theme-toggle" type="button" data-theme-toggle aria-pressed="false" aria-label="สลับเป็นโหมดกลางคืน"><span class="tt-night" aria-hidden="true">☾</span><span class="tt-day" aria-hidden="true">☀</span></button><button class="nav-toggle" type="button" data-nav-toggle aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="main-nav" aria-label="Open menu"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">☰</span></button><button class="icon-button" type="button" data-open-search aria-label="Search website (Press Ctrl+K)"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌕</span></button><a class="icon-button" href="/en/trip/" aria-label="Your trip"><span class="ib-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span><span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a><a class="header-map" href="/en/map/">Open map ↗</a></div></header><main id="main"><div class="stories-index-v2"><div class="intro"><a class="eyebrow" href="/en/">Takua Pa 101 / Old Town Guide</a><h1>Takua Pa Stories</h1><p class="lead">Four perspectives for reading the town through its sources · Getting to know the town, old houses and architecture, waterways and trade, people and flavors</p></div><div class="story-grid-v2"><article class="story-card-v2 story-card-v2-lead"><div class="card-art-v2"><img src="/assets/riverwalk.webp" width="1000" height="1000" alt="" loading="lazy"></div><div class="card-content-v2"><span class="chapter">Know the city</span><h2><a href="/en/stories/city/">Takua Pa: The Town That Moved with the River</a></h2><p>From an ancient settlement on the trans-peninsular route to a market and mining town · Verified facts and questions waiting to be answered.</p><div class="card-meta-v2"><span class="story-mins">6 minutes</span><span class="card-go" aria-hidden="true">Open this story ↗</span></div></div></article><article class="story-card-v2"><div class="card-art-v2"><img src="/assets/culture-street.webp" width="1000" height="1000" alt="" loading="lazy"></div><div class="card-content-v2"><span class="chapter">Old houses and architecture</span><h2><a href="/en/stories/architecture/">Buildings built with tin money and dredger steel · Architecture that remembers the town</a></h2><p>Read Takua Pa through the shophouses on Culture Street, Boon Sung Iron Bridge, the governor's residence, and Tao Ming School · The transition embedded in brick, mortar, and steel structures</p><div class="card-meta-v2"><span class="story-mins">6 minutes</span><span class="card-go" aria-hidden="true">Open this story ↗</span></div></div></article><article class="story-card-v2"><div class="card-art-v2"><img src="/assets/iron-bridge.webp" width="1000" height="1000" alt="" loading="lazy"></div><div class="card-content-v2"><span class="chapter">Waterways and trade</span><h2><a href="/en/stories/water-trade/">From Thung Tuk to the Takua Pa River: The Day the Waterway Built the Town</a></h2><p>The river is not just a backdrop. It is a route, a connector of people, and the determiner of the town's fate, which had to relocate due to sedimentation.</p><div class="card-meta-v2"><span class="story-mins">7 minutes</span><span class="card-go" aria-hidden="true">Open this story ↗</span></div></div></article><article class="story-card-v2"><div class="card-art-v2"><img src="/assets/food-center.webp" width="1000" height="1000" alt="" loading="lazy"></div><div class="card-content-v2"><span class="chapter">People and flavors</span><h2><a href="/en/stories/food-people/">Flavours of the Baba Community and the Old Market</a></h2><p>Food serves as both household memories and evidence of cultural exchange · Read Takua Pa through the Baba cuisine, double-layered Tao Sor, and the Culture Street</p><div class="card-meta-v2"><span class="story-mins">7 minutes</span><span class="card-go" aria-hidden="true">Open this story ↗</span></div></div></article><article class="story-card-v2"><div class="card-art-v2"><img src="/assets/tao-ming.webp" width="1000" height="667" alt="" loading="lazy"></div><div class="card-content-v2"><span class="chapter">City topics</span><h2><a href="/en/stories/kuapapoh/">Kuapapoh: The Day Old Houses Stand Up to Tell Their Stories</a></h2><p>A creative space project that revived houses number 78, 109, and 305 · What the new generation tells about the town, and what history still needs to uncover</p><div class="card-meta-v2"><span class="story-mins">6 minutes</span><span class="card-go" aria-hidden="true">Open this story ↗</span></div></div></article></div><aside class="source"><h2>How to read this page</h2><p>This article was compiled from official documents and academic-institution databases, with the evidence level identified for each topic · Check shop details, opening hours, and schedules with providers before travelling</p></aside></div></main><footer class="site-footer"><div class="footer-top"><a href="/en/" class="footer-name">Takua Pa <em>101</em></a><p>One city<br>Stories to get to know</p><a class="round-link" href="#main" aria-label="Back to top">↑</a></div><div class="footer-bottom"><a href="https://siwaracafe.com/">Created by Baan Siwara, Takua Pa</a><span>Old Town Guide · Phang Nga Province</span><a href="https://www.takuapacity.go.th/pdf/travel-preview.pdf">Original Brochure ↗</a></div></footer><nav class="tabbar" aria-label="Quick menu"><a href="/en/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span>Home</a><a href="/en/map/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◈</span>Map</a><a href="/en/eat/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Eat</a><a href="/en/trip/"><span class="tb-glyph" aria-hidden="true">◫</span>Trip<span class="qs-badge" data-trip-count hidden>0</span></a></nav></body></html>
